r" href=3D"https://aws.amazon.com/intellij/" data-sourcepos=3D"238:57-238:1=
00" target=3D"_blank">IntelliJ</a>, <a rel=3D"nofollow noreferrer noopener"=
 href=3D"https://aws.amazon.com/visualstudiocode/" data-sourcepos=3D"238:10=
3-238:164" target=3D"_blank">Visual Studio Code</a>, <a rel=3D"nofollow nor=
eferrer noopener" href=3D"https://aws.amazon.com/visualstudio/" data-source=
pos=3D"238:167-238:219" target=3D"_blank">Visual Studio</a>, <a rel=3D"nofo=
llow noreferrer noopener" href=3D"https://aws.amazon.com/cloud9/" data-sour=
cepos=3D"238:222-238:265" target=3D"_blank">AWS Cloud9</a>
</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"239:5-239:81">Build: <a rel=3D"nofollow noreferrer no=
opener" href=3D"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/" da=
ta-sourcepos=3D"239:14-239:81" target=3D"_blank">CodeBuild</a>
</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"240:5-240:151">Deploy: <a rel=3D"nofollow noreferrer =
noopener" href=3D"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/"=
 data-sourcepos=3D"240:15-240:84" target=3D"_blank">CodeDeploy</a>, <a rel=
=3D"nofollow noreferrer noopener" href=3D"https://wiki.jenkins.io/display/J=
ENKINS/AWS+SAM+Plugin" data-sourcepos=3D"240:87-240:151" target=3D"_blank">=
Jenkins</a>
</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"241:5-241:111">Continuous Delivery Pipelines: <a rel=
=3D"nofollow noreferrer noopener" href=3D"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codep=
ipeline/latest/userguide/" data-sourcepos=3D"241:38-241:111" target=3D"_bla=
nk">CodePipeline</a>
</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"242:5-243:0">Discover Serverless Apps &amp; Patterns:=
 <a rel=3D"nofollow noreferrer noopener" href=3D"https://docs.aws.amazon.co=
m/serverlessrepo/latest/devguide/" data-sourcepos=3D"242:44-242:143" target=
=3D"_blank">AWS Serverless Application Repository</a>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"244:1-245:0">
<p data-sourcepos=3D"244:4-244:326"><strong data-sourcepos=3D"244:4-244:30"=
>Built-in best practices</strong>. You can use SAM to define and deploy you=
r infrastructure as configuration. This makes it possible for you to use an=
d enforce best practices through code reviews. Also, with a few lines of co=
nfiguration, you can enable safe deployments through CodeDeploy, and can en=
able tracing using AWS X-Ray.</p>
</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"246:1-247:0">
<p data-sourcepos=3D"246:4-246:363"><strong data-sourcepos=3D"246:4-246:38"=
>Extension of AWS CloudFormation</strong>. Because SAM is an extension of A=
WS CloudFormation, you get the reliable deployment capabilities of AWS Clou=
dFormation. You can define resources by using CloudFormation in your SAM te=
mplate. Also, you can use the full suite of resources, intrinsic functions,=
 and other template features that are available in CloudFormation.</p>
</li>
</ol>
